 ## Background
-The method originates from direct volume ray casting techniques that utilize jittered sampling to mitigate aliasing. The specific implementation details, including the jitter texture lookup and Phong shading integration, are documented in the VoxViz thesis [S1, unofficial]. Consistent sampling across subvolumes for parallel rendering was discussed in early parallel ray tracing algorithms [S3].
